fix: correct runtime and training defects found during verification

Fixes the working bugs listed in FIXES.md: missing test package __init__ and
encoder forward(), absent torch.nn.functional import, stale computation graph
leaking through the query cache, 768-d native projection versus 512-d token
states separation, dot-fusion width rebuilt on every call, token-interaction
dimensions and padding masks, confidence dimensions for two-candidate lists,
chunking tokenizer handling and truncation reporting, duplicate document ids in
results, order-independent graded relevance in the pairwise loss, padding
excluded from listwise and distillation targets, ragged-batch encoding, default
backbone freezing, LoRA named-parameter checks, and the final optimizer step on
gradient accumulation.

Also corrects the upstream text attention head count in the docs to 4.

Verified with Python 3.12.14, PyTorch 2.14.1+cpu, Transformers 5.19.0,
pytest 9.1.1: 140 tests pass, smoke training passes, and all three inference
examples run against the real google/embeddinggemma-2 backbone.
